      "side": 1,
      "message": "why did we switch to generating random bytes in SHA256_DIGEST_SIZE increments? iiuc PS_len is always under a dozen bytes, so going byte-by-byte (as before) might be better. it is fips_rand_bytes, not fips_trng_bytes, so even fips_rand_bytes(r, 1) should be ok. or can do fips_rand_bytes(padded, PS_len), then scan for 0s, and starting with the first zero do fips_rand_bytes(padded, PS_len - index_of_zero).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
